{
 "about": "A value said as a share of its range, as TalkBack and VoiceOver say a progress bar or a slider (docs/adr/0039-keyboard-access.mdx): sample/ValueShareProbe.tsx, the screen reader on in Spanish. An element whose accessibilityValue gives a number between a minimum and a maximum and no words is published and said with its share of that range, in the session's locale (\"25 %\": 50 of 0 to 200, 15 of 10 to 30), never the raw number; its words win (\"3 de 10 archivos\"). Bloom's Meter is a level indicator (`meter`) and, with role=\"progressbar\", a progress indicator, each with its share as Bloom formats it. A slider stepped by the arrows says its new share once, nothing at the top of its range. At 1.25 (1600 × 1000).",
 "module": "ValueShareProbe",
 "window": [
  480,
  320
 ],
